From 7db067466ae8eefab98144b83b506deb790eb28a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:45:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] engine: spec lanes for two users beside the slot groups
 (opt-in STRATA_SPEC_LANES=2)

When exactly the two lane slots decode (0 and GS: where the server puts the
first two users with pipelined groups), each runs as its own solo-MTP stream
instead of a one-row group window: its own verifier per stage bound to the
slot's sessions (sized like the solo verifier, set_always_publish), its own
drafter (--batch-mtp's slot drafter: the solo drafter's weights, own K/V),
windows moved stage to stage as each finishes (the two lanes share one
stream per stage, so their windows interleave on every card), the verdict on
the last stage (exact match, Philox(seed, pos)), the commit queued on every
stage at once (eager), per-window completion by event, the chain for the
next window.  Any line but BSTOP drains the lanes (as it drains the groups),
and so does a broken gate; otherwise the batch pump runs as before.

- gate (spec_lanes.hpp): both lane slots active, nothing else, each request
  lane_ok (no penalties, no logit bias, no pictures); STRATA_SPEC_LANES_ONE=1
  also keeps a lone lane.  Not with --batch-mtp, --adapt-async, --mtp-q4,
  helper caches, coupled/prob drafts, mtp on the first card.
- a verdict emits per token with the pump's checks and commits exactly the
  rows whose picks went out, so a finished slot is a conversation cache as
  the pump leaves it; STRATA_SLOT_PARK captures it once the commits landed.
- Verifier::set_rope_base (lane verifiers only; 0 elsewhere): solo windows on
  a slot session rotate in the slot's M-RoPE region, as its batch rows do.
  The lane slots' first-stage sessions get the main PleRun with their own
  history (what the batch rows read).
- drafts: the admission's draft K/V into the lane drafter (and back to the
  solo drafter when a request continues the slot, STRATA_SPEC_LANES_GIVEBACK),
  first drafts from the admission's last row (merged windows included), a
  T=1 catch-up from every pump/batch_step row of a lane slot
  (STRATA_SPEC_LANES_CATCHUP=0: off).  Drafts never change tokens.
- the last stage runs one lane window at a time (a sampled verdict syncs its
  stream); the drafter's card runs chains and last-stage windows in arrival
  order (STRATA_SPEC_LANES_SERIAL3=0: side by side).
- VRAM: 2 x 200 MiB per card kept out of the expert caches when asked; a
  per-card room check before allocating, costs said per card at boot and at
  the first lane start (graphs).  kLiveMax 16 -> 32 (#267 release registry).
- logs: INFO spec_lanes=2 lane_slots=a,b; a line per lane run (tokens, tok/s,
  acceptance, catch-ups); STRATA_SPEC_LANES_LOG=1 a line per start.
- test spec_lanes_test (CPU).
Off (default): kernels SASS-identical, host default branches unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
